{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":288930,"duration_api_ms":337365,"num_turns":41,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"23d3495f-ea8a-4055-a704-582d5c4a84fa","total_cost_usd":1.8726670499999998,"usage":{"input_tokens":1361,"cache_creation_input_tokens":71394,"cache_read_input_tokens":1966987,"output_tokens":8409,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":71394,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":1361,"outputTokens":8409,"cacheReadInputTokens":1966987,"cacheCreationInputTokens":71394,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.646736,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000},"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":1716,"outputTokens":9506,"cacheReadInputTokens":537588,"cacheCreationInputTokens":98341,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.22593105000000002,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"amendments":[{"body":"Add a comment to the `system:habitat_registry_finalize` stage in `crates/tank_core/src/engine.rs` (around line 376-382) explaining WHY a second refresh is needed: `update_daily_filter_clogging` modifies `filter_state.clogging_index`, which `compute_filter_media` reads (habitat.rs:164) to compute FilterMedia oxygen exposure. Without this comment, the dual-refresh pattern looks redundant and a future contributor may remove it, silently introducing stale clogging data in the serialized registry.","rationale":"The first habitat refresh (line 355) captures plant/algae/microfauna changes; the second (line 380) captures clogging_index changes from filter clogging. This dependency chain is non-obvious and the finalize stage currently has no explanatory comment, making it fragile against future refactoring."},{"body":"In `crates/tank_core/src/engine.rs` line 727, the unconditional `self.state.refresh_habitat_registry()` at the end of `process_action` runs after every player action including `Feed`, `AddShrimp`, `RemoveShrimp`, and `SiphonDetritus`, none of which modify habitat-relevant state (geometry, hardware, plants, substrate, or filter). Consider either (a) making the refresh conditional on action type, or (b) adding a brief comment explaining that the unconditional approach is an intentional simplicity-over-performance trade-off. This prevents future confusion about whether the unconditional call is deliberate or an oversight.","rationale":"The habitat computation is cheap (5 habitats, all arithmetic), so this is not a performance bug. But without a comment, the unconditional call after Feed/AddShrimp/RemoveShrimp looks like an oversight. A one-line comment documenting the design choice would suffice."}],"summary":"Reviewed all changes in the d1246de..9f7f910 range for tanksim-6e5.5.1-v2. The core habitat registry changes are correct and well-tested: `refresh_habitat_registry()` centralization ensures no stale state, bounds clamping (`.clamp(0.0, 1.0)` for modifiers, `.max(0.0)` for areas) is properly applied in `compute_habitat_registry`, save-load always rebuilds the registry on deserialization, and comprehensive tests verify from_parts refresh, post-trim-action freshness, daily-update freshness, and startup-override freshness. The dual daily refresh stages are functionally justified (the second captures `clogging_index` changes from `update_daily_filter_clogging`). All tests pass. The ancillary changes (preset microfauna/death routing fields, TUI legacy snapshot normalization, provenance param normalization) are also correct — partition sums validated, legacy field priority is canonical > legacy, and non-finite values are safely preserved. Two minor documentation amendments proposed; no correctness bugs found."},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"d1e499af-e1e9-4c13-8f46-4964759f6644"}
